#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:2
msgid "Use resource quotas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:4
msgid ""
"A quota group sets resource limits on {ref}`services <how-to-guides-manage-"
"snaps-control-services>` running inside snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:6
msgid "Resource limits can be set for the following attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:7
msgid ""
"**Journal log messages**: as a maximum size for the log and as a rate limit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:8
msgid "**Memory**: as a maximum amount of RAM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:9
msgid ""
"**CPU usage**: as a percentage across a number - or specific - CPU cores, "
"and as a given number of threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:11
msgid ""
"Quota groups are created, removed and queried with the following _snap_ "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:13
msgid "**set-quota**: create or update a quota group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:14
msgid "**quota**: show quota group for a set of snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:15
msgid "**quotas**: show all quota groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:16
msgid "**remove-quota**: remove a quota group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:18
msgid ""
"Quota groups require snap version _2.59+_. Setting quotas for journal log "
"messages is currently considered experimental and requires that an "
"*experimental feature-flag* is first be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:20
msgid "sudo snap set system experimental.quota-groups=true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:24
msgid "Create a quota group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:26
msgid ""
"To create a quota group, use the `snap set-quota` command with a group name "
"and a limiting attribute, such as `--memory=<amount>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:28
msgid "`snap set-quota mygroup --memory=64MB`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:30
msgid "Add snaps to a quota group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:32
msgid ""
"Snaps that contain services can be optionally added to a quota group when a "
"group is created:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:34
msgid "`snap set-quota mygroup --memory=64MB snap1 snap2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:36
msgid ""
"After a group has been created, a snap can be added to a group when it's "
"installed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:38
msgid "`snap install snap1 --quota-group=mygroup`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:40
msgid ""
"A pre-installed snap can be added to a pre-existing quota group by running "
"the `set-quota` command again:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:42
msgid "`snap set-quota highmem hello-world`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:44
msgid ""
"See below for details on which limiting attributes are supported by quota "
"groups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:46
msgid "Limiting attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:49
msgid "Journal log limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:51
msgid ""
"While the `snap logs` command is used to retrieve the _systemd journal_ logs "
"for a specific service, or for all services within a snap (see {ref}"
"`Inspecting logs <ref-control-services_inspecting-logs>` for further "
"details), a quota can be used to limit the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:53
msgid "Log output can be limited by both size and rate within a quota group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:55
msgid "Journal size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:57
msgid "`journal-size=<value>[KB|MB|GB]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:59
msgid ""
"Limit the size of the aggregated journal log for all the snaps in the quota "
"group. This is useful when service log output is verbose on devices with "
"limited storage capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:61
msgid ""
"Accepts a value in either kilobytes(KB), megabytes(MB) or gigabytes(GB), "
"including aggregated values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:63
msgid "sudo snap set-quota loggroup --journal-size=64MB\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:67
msgid "Journal rate limit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:69
msgid "`journal-rate-limit=<number-of-messages>/<time-period>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:71
msgid ""
"Limit the number of messages logged to a maximum per time period. This is a "
"useful way of limiting the number of messages for snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:73
msgid ""
"The time period can be milliseconds (ms), seconds(s), minutes (m), and "
"hours(h), including aggregated periods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:75
msgid "sudo snap set-quota loggroup --journal-rate-limit=10/1h2m3s4ms5us\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:79
msgid "Memory limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:81
msgid "`memory=value[KB|MB|GB]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:83
msgid ""
"Memory units can be 'B', 'KB', 'MB or 'GB' with a size greater than 4KB:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:85
msgid "sudo snap set-quota highmem --memory=2GB\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:89
msgid ""
"The memory limit for a quota group can only be increased.  Increasing the "
"memory limit for a quota group *does not* restart any services associated "
"with snaps in the quota group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:91
msgid ""
"To decrease the memory limit for a quota group, the entire group must be "
"removed with the _remove-quota_ command and recreated with a lower limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:93
msgid "CPU limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:95
msgid ""
"CPU limits can be set in 4 different ways, some of which can be combined "
"depending on requirements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:97
#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:104
msgid "Percentage of total CPU resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:98
#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:109
msgid "Percentage of a given number of CPU cores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:99
#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:118
msgid "Percentage for specific cores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:100
msgid "Limit the number of threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:102
msgid ""
"Without a specified CPU limit, all quota groups can use the full system "
"capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:105
msgid "`cpu=<percentage>%`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:107
msgid ""
"Sets a relative percentage limit on how much execution time a process "
"receives, regardless of the number of cores available, up to 100%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:110
msgid "`--cpu=<number of cores>x<percentage>%`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:112
msgid ""
"<!-- TODO: this behaviour is on systems using cgroupsv2 (grep ^cgroup /etc/"
"mtab).  Without this, CPU limits use CPUQuota (200% means two cores). This "
"needs to be tested and documented. -->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:114
msgid ""
"One or more cores can be specified alongside a CPU percentage to allocate "
"relative CPU resources across only that number of cores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:116
msgid ""
"For example, `--cpu=2x100%` on a 4 core system would permit a process to run "
"at full capacity on only two cores, which is equivalent to 50% of full "
"system capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:120
msgid "`cpu-set=<core number 1>,<core number 2> --cpu=<percentage>%`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:122
msgid ""
"Using an additional `--cpu-set` argument with `--cpu` , it's possible to "
"specify exactly which cores to be used as the CPU resources for that quota "
"group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:124
msgid ""
"For example, `--cpu-set=0,1 --cpu=100%` will permit up to 100% CPU resource "
"usage on 2 specific cores (0 and 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:126
msgid ""
"The following example will allow up to a maximum of half usage combined on "
"four specific cores which means the sum of usage across all 4 specific cores "
"cannot exceed 200%:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:128
msgid "snap set-quota max-two-specific-cores --cpu-set=0,1,2,3 --cpu=50%\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:132
msgid ""
"In the above example, services in the _max-two-specific-cores_ quota group "
"could run using 100% of two cores and 0% of the other two cores, or 25% of "
"each core, 33% of 3 of the cores and 0% of the last core, or any other "
"combination that does not exceed 200%. The number 200% comes from the size "
"of the `--cpu-set` set multiplied by the `--cpu` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:134
msgid "4. Limit the number of threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:136
msgid "`threads=<thread limit>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:138
msgid ""
"The `--threads` option is used to limit the number of threads or processes "
"that can be created by the snaps within the quota group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:140
msgid ""
"For example, `--threads=4096` will limit a quota group to no more than 4096 "
"threads or processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:142
msgid ""
"The _threads_ option can also be used with both `--cpu` and `--cpu-set` "
"options to target specific requirements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:144
msgid ""
"snap set-quota max-two-specific-cores --cpu-set=0,1,2,3 --cpu=50% --"
"threads=8092\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:148
msgid ""
"By default, quota groups are not limited in the number of threads they can "
"create."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:151
msgid "View quotas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:153
msgid ""
"If the group already exists, _set-quota_ will update its resource limits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:155
msgid "Use the _quotas_ command to view created quota groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:157
msgid ""
"$ snap quotas\n"
"Quota      Parent  Constraints                        Current\n"
"highmem            memory=2.00GB cpu=50%,cpu-set=0,1\n"
"cpuhalf            cpu=50%,cpu-set=0,1\n"
"manycores          cpu=2x,cpu=100%,threads=4096\n"
"maxcores           cpu=100%\n"
"memcpu             memory=2.00GB,cpu=50%\n"
"threads            threads=4096\n"
"loggroup           journal-size=64.0MB,journal-rate=10/1h2m3.004005s\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:168
msgid ""
"Snaps can belong to only one quota group, but quota groups can be nested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:170
msgid "Nested quota groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:172
msgid ""
"To create a nested quota group, add the `--parent=<parent group>` argument "
"to the _set-quota_ command when creating a new quota group:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:174
msgid "sudo snap set-quota lowmem --memory=1GB --parent=highmem\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:178
msgid "The *quotas* command will also show nested quota groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:180
msgid ""
"$ snap quotas\n"
"Quota    Parent   Constraints    Current\n"
"highmem           memory=2.00GB  \n"
"lowmem   highmem  memory=1.00GB  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:186
msgid ""
"The total resource use of nested quota groups cannot exceed that of the "
"parent group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:188
msgid "Update a quota group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:190
msgid ""
"Add the names of one or more snaps to the _set-quota_ command to include "
"those snaps in the quota group when its created:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:192
msgid "sudo snap set-quota lowmem go-example-webserver --parent=highmem\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:196
msgid ""
"If the quota group already exists, snaps can be added by using _set-quota_ "
"without the resource limit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:198
msgid "sudo snap set-quota lowmem go-example-webserver\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:202
msgid ""
"Adding new a snap to a quota group will result in all non-disabled services "
"in that snap being restarted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:205
msgid ""
"New quotas can be set on existing quota groups, but existing quotas cannot "
"be removed from a quota group, without removing and recreating the entire "
"group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:207
msgid ""
"The CPU set limit for a quota group can be modified to include new cores, or "
"to remove existing cores from the quota already set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:209
msgid ""
"The threads limit for a quota group can be increased but not decreased. To "
"decrease the _threads_ limit for a quota group, the entire group must be "
"removed with the remove-quota command and recreated with a lower limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:213
msgid ""
"Updating quotas in a group, or imposing new quotas on an existing quota "
"group, will per default require restarting any running services in that "
"quota group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:215
msgid "View group members and resource usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:217
msgid ""
"The _quota_ command shows information about a quota group, including the set "
"of  snaps it includes and any subgroups it contains, as well as its resource "
"constraints and  the current usage of those constrained resources by snap "
"services in those snaps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:221
msgid ""
"$ snap quota lowmem\n"
"name:    lowmem\n"
"parent:  highmem\n"
"constraints:\n"
"  memory:  1.00GB\n"
"current:\n"
"  memory:  5.32MB\n"
"snaps:\n"
"  - go-example-webserver\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:233
msgid ""
"Use the _quota_ command on the parent of any nested groups to view total "
"resource usage and subgroups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:235
msgid ""
"$ snap quota highmem\n"
"name:  highmem\n"
"constraints:\n"
"  memory:  2.00GB\n"
"current:\n"
"  memory:  5.35MB\n"
"subgroups:\n"
"  - lowmem\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:246
msgid "Remove snaps and quota groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:248
msgid ""
"To remove a snap from a quota group, the entire group must be removed with "
"the _remove-quota_ command and the quota group recreated without the snaps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:251
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap remove-quota lowmem\n"
"$ sudo snap set-quota lowmem --memory=1GB\n"
"$ snap quota lowmem\n"
"name:  lowmem\n"
"constraints:\n"
"  memory:  1.00GB\n"
"current:\n"
"  memory:  0B\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:262
msgid ""
"Currently, only quota groups with no subgroups can be removed. In order to "
"remove a quota group with subgroups, the subgroups must be first removed "
"until there are no further subgroups in the group, then the group itself can "
"be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:264
msgid "An existing subgroup cannot be moved from one parent to another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/use-resource-quotas.md:266
msgid ""
"To remove a subgroup from a quota group, the subgroup must be first removed "
"directly with the remove-quota command."
msgstr ""
